=========================================================================
2. CLAY MATHEMATICS INSTITUTE COMPLIANCE
=========================================================================
This repository is structured to satisfy the Clay Mathematics Institute
Millennium Prize Rules (adopted by the Board of Directors 26 Sept 2018,
https://www.claymath.org/millennium-problems/rules/ and
https://www.claymath.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/millennium_prize_rules_0.pdf).
The canonical official description for P vs NP is Cook (2000):
https://www.claymath.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/06/pvsnp.pdf

Per §4–§7 of the Rules, a Proposed Solution must satisfy ALL of:

  (a) Published in a Qualifying Outlet — a refereed mathematics publication
      of worldwide repute with: (i) named editorial board available for
      contact; (ii) editor(s) capable of identifying appropriate referees;
      (iii) published refereeing process ensuring review by appropriate
      experts; (iv) inclusion in MathSciNet. The relaxed route under §6(f)
      requires SAB recommendation and BOD approval. This repository alone
      is NOT a Qualifying Outlet and will not be considered a submission
      to CMI (§6.b, §7.a: no direct submission, no supplementary material).

  (b) At least two (2) years elapsed since publication in the Qualifying
      Outlet.

  (c) General acceptance in the global mathematics community, as determined
      in CMI's sole discretion (citations by independent researchers,
      international conferences, awards, detailed scrutiny — Notes on the
      Rules).

  (d) Satisfactorily answered the questions in the official Problem
      description, as determined by CMI. For P vs NP (§4.b), resolution
      in EITHER direction (P=NP or P≠NP) is evaluated by the standard
      procedure (§7): SAB constitutes a Special Advisory Committee
      (≥1 SAB member + ≥2 non-SAB international experts), each component
      verified by one or more members.

  (e) No entitlement to explanation of CMI's decision (§8).

Authors seeking Clay consideration must publish the mathematical content
through a Qualifying Outlet independently. This license explicitly permits
that path (see §3).

