3. DUAL LICENSING
=========================================================================
To simultaneously preserve sovereign ownership and enable Clay-qualifying
publication and independent verification, this repository uses a dual license:

  (A) MATHEMATICAL CONTENT — CC BY 4.0 + Apache 2.0 (Clay-Publication Track):
      Applies to: theorem statements, definitions, lemmas, problem
      descriptions, SharedFoundation/* (Spec.md, Alphabet.lean … ThreeSAT.lean,
      CommonSemantics.lean, ARCHITECTURE.md), HybridQuantumSAT/Basic/*,
      Bridge/* specifications, and any file bearing header "Licensed under
      CC BY 4.0 for Clay publication." You are granted a worldwide,
      royalty-free license to: reproduce, share, adapt, publish in a
      refereed journal or other Qualifying Outlet, deposit in arXiv/MathSciNet-
      indexed venues, cite, and verify — provided you give attribution:

        © 2026 Ahmad Ali Parr + Jessica Westerhoff, Bel Esprit d'Accord Trust
        Source: https://github.com/SNAPKITTYWEST/CLAY-INSTITUTE-P-VS-NP
        Fingerprint: SDC-Ω-∂-2026-PVSNP

      Attribution must appear in the publication and in any derivative
      mathematical exposition. No endorsement claim is permitted.

  (B) ENGINEERING IMPLEMENTATION — Sovereign Source License v1.0
      (Sovereign-Track):
      Applies to: execution infrastructure, orchestrators, cloud workers,
      proprietary kernels, non-mathematical tooling, and any file bearing
      header "Licensed under the SOVEREIGN SOURCE LICENSE v1.0".
      What is permitted: viewing on GitHub, citing theorem names/statements
      with attribution, submission to CMI via a Qualifying Outlet (which
      necessarily exercises the (A) grant for the mathematical content).
      What is forbidden without explicit written permission (jessicalw34@gmail.com):
        - forking for any purpose other than viewing
        - copying/extracting implementation code beyond fair-use citation
        - incorporating proof terms/structure into other proof libraries or software
        - commercial use, derivative works, distribution, ML training

  If a file does not specify (A) or (B), (A) applies to its mathematical
  content and (B) applies to its executable/engineering content.

